2:T662,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to fit a kitchen in London?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough UK guide, fitting-only labour may typically be around £3,000–£10,000, while a complete small-to-medium kitchen renovation may typically fall around £8,000–£25,000. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average cost of a new kitchen in London?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough UK guide, a modest complete kitchen may start from around £8,000, a mid-range renovation may typically be around £15,000–£30,000, and larger or premium projects may exceed £30,000. Every project differs; confirm whether a quote includes appliances, VAT, removal and finishing work, and request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is kitchen fitting separate from the cost of the kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be. The kitchen price may cover cabinets, doors and sometimes a worktop, while fitting covers installation. Plumbing, electrical work, tiling, flooring, disposal and decorating may be separate unless clearly included."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes kitchen installation more expensive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Moving plumbing or electrical points, removing walls, choosing stone worktops, repairing walls or floors, replacing appliances and working in a difficult-to-access property can all increase the final cost."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitting-cost-london","d"]
